\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Wick powers under blocking}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{Let #{Q} be a positive hierarchical precision at depth #{k\ge1},
and let #{Q'=\Phi_{\lambda,k}(Q)} under the
\vocabk{blocking step}{fdip-01CJ}. Write #{c_0>0} for its eigenvalue
on #{\im P_0^{(k)}}. Let #{\sigma^2} and #{\tau^2} be the site
variances of the centered Gaussian probabilities of #{Q} and #{Q'}.
Then
##{\sigma^2=\frac{\tau^2}{p\lambda}+v,
\qquad v=c_0^{-1}(1-p^{-1}).}
For every integer #{n\ge0}, the canonical conditional Gaussian
probability given #{T_k\xi=y} satisfies, at every #{y\in F_{k-1}},
##{\mathbb E\left[
\sum_{x\in X_k}{:\xi(x)^n:}_{\sigma^2}\,\middle|\,T_k\xi=y\right]
=p(p\lambda)^{-n/2}
\sum_{r\in X_{k-1}}{:y(r)^n:}_{\tau^2}.}
The colon expressions are the \vocabk{Wick powers}{fdip-01CV}.}

\p{Consequently, on any \vocabk{tower}{fdip-01CJ}, the polynomial
observables
##{U_{n,k}(x)=\sum_{a\in X_k}{:x(a)^n:}_{\sigma_k^2}}
form a \vocabk{scaling direction}{fdip-01CQ} for the
conditional-expectation step, with positive eigenvalue
#{p(p\lambda)^{-n/2}}. The variance #{\sigma_k^2} is that of
the actual reference probability at depth #{k}.}

\proof{
\p{The retained and fluctuation fields are independent by
\ref{fdip-01CH}, since #{Q} commutes with #{E_1^{(k)}}.
Write #{\zeta=P_0^{(k)}\xi}. The conditional field at a given
#{y} is
##{\xi=\frac{S_ky}{\sqrt{p\lambda}}+\zeta.}
Indeed #{E_1^{(k)}\xi=S_kA_k\xi} and
#{A_k\xi=y/\sqrt{p\lambda}}; the independent fluctuation keeps
its original Gaussian probability. Its covariance on the fine space
is #{c_0^{-1}P_0^{(k)}}. In the counting basis, the diagonal of
#{P_0^{(k)}=\bbI -E_1^{(k)}} is #{1-p^{-1}}, so every
#{\zeta(x)} has variance #{v}. The block value at site #{x} has
variance #{\tau^2/(p\lambda)}. Independence adds these two
variances, proving the first display. The site variances are uniform
by \ref{fdip-009B}; at depth zero there is only one site.}

\p{For a site #{x=r+tp^{k-1}}, put
#{u=y(r)/\sqrt{p\lambda}} and #{s=\tau^2/(p\lambda)}.
The smoothing identity in \ref{fdip-01CX} gives
##{\mathbb E{: (u+\zeta(x))^n:}_{s+v}
={:u^n:}_s
=(p\lambda)^{-n/2}{:y(r)^n:}_{\tau^2},}
where the last equality is its scaling identity. There are #{p}
sites with this coarse label #{r}. Summing proves the claimed
conditional expectation. Only finite sums and finite polynomial
moments occur. The formula remains valid at #{n=0}, when each fine
site contributes one.}

\p{For a tower, #{Q'} is the next reference precision by definition,
so the formula is exactly the stated identity for consecutive
observables #{U_{n,k}}. Each observable is a nonzero polynomial:
its highest-degree part is the sum of the #{n}-th powers of the
coordinates, and for #{n=0} it is the positive number #{p^k}.}
}
